{"repositoryId":1011002355,"availability":"available","full":"cariboulabs/cler","name":"cler","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":6,"forks":2,"created":"2025-06-30T06:49:34Z","updated":"2026-10-18T08:40:18Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://cariboulabs.github.io/cler/demos/run/earshot/index.html","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T19:18:59.783Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T19:18:59.783Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T19:18:59.783Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T19:18:59.783Z","stars":6,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Onboarding page · Try cler-fg in your browser","CLER is a C++ template-based framework for constructing and executing flowgraphs of DSP processing blocks. Its goal is to keep a tiny header only core allowing maximal flexibility:","But embedded devices dont need DSP do they? Embedded Linux aside, most embedded devices traditionally relied on dedicated chips — for fusion, filtering, or modulation. But with today’s powerful SoCs and the rise of agentic AI, it’s often faster, cheaper, and more flexible to move DSP into software. CLER aims to fill that gap."],"features":["Defining blocks amounts to implementing a struct with a method","Channels are type agnostic","Blocks are not limited by number of input/output Channels","Callbacks can be used for communication between unconnected blocks","Flowgraphs and Blocks can be made almost completely static"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cariboulabs/cler/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f87cf7fe41434346595fcf9faa549e92e51516fc5385b40afc1bfde2f195d19c","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T19:18:59.902Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T19:18:59.902Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Onboarding page · Try cler-fg in your browser","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cariboulabs/cler/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirement